## 1. Schema + migration
Add a Shop model:
- id (cuid), name (unique, or unique per user if auth exists), icon (optional emoji), color (default "#6366f1"), isDefault (bool), isArchived (bool, default false), createdAt, updatedAt, transactions relation
- If auth exists, add userId with relation and index.

On Transaction:
- Add shopId with relation to Shop, onDelete: Restrict
- Add @@index([shopId, date]) (use the actual date field name)

Migration requirements:
- Create a default shop ("Main Shop", isDefault = true) inside the migration SQL.
- Backfill ALL existing transactions to that default shop.
- After backfill, shopId must be NOT NULL (required in Prisma).
- Do NOT seed shops lazily inside a GET handler.

## 2. Shops API
- GET /api/shops: list non-archived shops (support ?includeArchived=true), default first.
- POST /api/shops: create. Validate name (non-empty, trimmed, unique) and color (hex). If isDefault = true, unset others in the same prisma.$transaction.
- PUT /api/shops/[id]: update name/icon/color/isDefault/isArchived with the same validation and single-default rule.
- DELETE /api/shops/[id]:
  - Reject (409) if the shop has transactions; tell the user to archive instead.
  - Reject deleting or archiving the last active shop.
  - If deleting or archiving the default shop, promote another active shop to default.
- Exactly one default shop must exist at all times. Enforce in code; on Postgres also add a partial unique index on isDefault WHERE isDefault = true.
- If auth exists, enforce ownership on every route.

## 3. Transaction and related APIs
- GET transactions, overview, analytics, dashboard summaries, and exports accept an optional shopId query param. No shopId = all shops (backwards compatible).
- POST/PUT transactions require shopId. Server-side, validate the shop exists, is not archived, and belongs to the user.
- PUT allows changing shopId (moving an entry between shops).
- Opening/closing/carried-forward balances must be computed per shop when shopId is given, and across all shops when it isn't.
- Include shop { id, name, color, icon } in transaction list responses so the UI can show it.
- Ask me whether categories should be shared or per-shop before changing them. Default: shared.

## 4. ShopProvider (frontend)
- Context exposing: shops, activeShopId ("all" or a shop id), setActiveShopId, refreshShops, isLoading.
- Place it in a layout that wraps BOTH the transactions pages and analytics.
- Persist the selection in localStorage, read it inside useEffect (avoid SSR hydration mismatch).
- If the stored id no longer exists or is archived, fall back to the default shop.
- Default selection on first visit: the default shop.

## 5. Shop switcher
- Prominent pill/tab bar at the top of the Daily Kanakku page: colored dot + icon + name per shop, plus an "All Shops" pill.
- Horizontally scrollable on mobile.
- Hide the switcher entirely when only one active shop exists.

## 6. Transactions UI
- Pass activeShopId to all transaction/overview API calls (omit the param when "all").
- Include shopId in all SWR/React Query keys (or refetch on change) so no stale data shows after switching.
- TransactionModal:
  - Shop picker field, pre-filled with the active shop.
  - When the active view is "All Shops", the picker is required with no preselection.
  - Editing an entry allows changing its shop.
- In the "All Shops" view, show the shop's colored dot/name on each transaction row.

## 7. Settings: Shops section
- List shops with name, icon, color, default badge, archived state.
- Add/edit form: name, emoji icon, color picker (offer ~8 preset colors).
- Actions: Set as default, Archive/Unarchive, Delete (show the API's 409 message clearly).
- After any change, call refreshShops() from the provider.

## 8. Analytics
- Analytics pages read activeShopId from the provider and pass it to the API.
- Show which shop is being viewed in the page header.

